# tally 2.1.8 item 77 (#201), E §4.1 step 2 and L §4.4: a test of a window-dated movement that comes out one way on
# some of its days and another on the rest is the window's hole, as far as the refusal or the other class would reach.
# out takes 100.00 PLN from jar (min 0, 50.00 PLN) on a day of window(03-05, 03-10), inn brings 100.00 PLN on 03-07:
# on 03-05 and 03-06 jar breaks its sign rule, on the rest it holds, so p1 is the hole and p2 splits it. 2.1.7's
# refcore booked out on the window's last day only (50.00 PLN). The plan's c5s.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
place jar: savings lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input wd: date
input dd: date

move out: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from jar to world amount amt

move inn: transfers
  on dd
  leg cash from world to jar amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  wd = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) "s"
  dd = 2026-03-07 "s"
  opening[jar] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask p1: bal(jar, 2026-03-31)
ask p2: bal(jar, 2026-03-31) windows each
=== expect
p1: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) not precise enough for a balance" (out)
  cut 2026-01-01
p2 [wd = 2026-03-05]: refused: RUN-PLACE jar is -50.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-03-05
  cut 2026-01-01
p2 [wd = 2026-03-06]: refused: RUN-PLACE jar is -50.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-03-06
  cut 2026-01-01
p2 [wd = 2026-03-07 .. 2026-03-10]: 50.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
